Z||000000||danny boy||06-16-2001||03:24 AM|||| I think I will put a sunroof in the GT. Here's the problem: I went to the local Upullit yard and took the whole roof panel from an 85 SE. I was as carefull as I could be not to break the apillars. I was looking for something else and just happened upon this. After an hour and a half I managed to get it in one piece. I took it to the register and paid for it,took it to the car, then remembered I had the car. Hmmm...<BR> I had already paid for it and since a fiero roof panel won't exactly fit in an Eclipse, I got mad and just broke the A pillars down off.<BR> So, has anyone ever used just the top of the panel and glassed the A pillars together? I know its awfully thin and the car does flex a goods deal. Just wonderin if it will work.<P>------------------<BR>don't push the A/c button.. it catches the car on fire        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PFF_sig_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bluebottlejunky||06-16-2001||11:30 AM||||um ya, i have heard of it befor..there was a post not to long ago about it.  BTW how much did you pay?<P><P>------------------<BR>Hello, My name is Mike and I am addicted too fiero's...PLEASE dont help me.<BR>85'GT 4sp<BR>AIM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||1
Z||000002||Galen||06-16-2001||12:03 PM||||My brother glassed(or something) in a sunroof out of a 84 se into a 88 S15.. looked sweet..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> one of a kind I do say. Twas a beautiful purple too, just like my car<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/redcreature.gif">     <BR> <A HREF="mailto:galen@spinrpg.com">galen@spinrpg.com</A>  -<A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe w/ sunroof</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - <A HREF="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>WebJolt Pictures</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||danny boy||06-16-2001||12:59 PM|||| For the roof panel,Glass and mounting hardware, It came to a grand total of $35.00.<BR>That was the only one they had,though.||||reg||1
Z||000004||cadaver||06-16-2001||01:12 PM||||I would probably glass the a pillars back on. not try to glass the roof to your a pillars. mount them both to the car for alignment then do the glass work||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||06-16-2001||01:20 PM||||Sounds like you should have a pretty clean break... Epoxy the sections back together with "plastic welder" epoxy. If need be glass a little on the back for strength. All you should need on the front after that is some sopt filler and a bit of sanding.<P>The plastic welder epoxy is tough stuff and it's made for just these kinds of materials. It sticks well to everything but the nose and tail soft panels. Odds are good that if you are careful putting it together the crack will hardly show.<P>Yes, the car flexes, but keep in mind that the flex is spread over the whole pillar. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Master_Sushi||06-16-2001||06:05 PM||||I will be epoxying another roof together soon. Im still in the process of switching the roofs from my 84se to my 88 coupe I just finished geting the roof from the black 84se glued back together,sanded,and nicely painted. Last night I was taking the roof off my perfect white 88, hoping to take it off in one piece and it broke! Not just in the pillers! The windshield must have been replaced at some time because the roof was REALLY stuck near the windshield with this hard yellow glue. It was so hard to get off I ended up taking it out in about 5 pieces. THEN I somehow lightly nicked the windshield with a screwdriver and I put a big crack in my windshield   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> ! Im going to try and get the roof bonded back together (this roof is going back on my black84) but im not 100% I can. If I knew it was going to be this much of a PITA to swap the roofs I would have never bothered. Glass man comes monday to put a new windshield in both my fieros   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">. You dont want to know what my 84s windshield looks like now. Its in about as many pieces as my white roof. lol... someone tell me it will all be ok   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 06-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Songman||06-16-2001||06:22 PM||||It will! It'll be just fine! If nothing else, I am sure there are fine folks on this forum that can sell you a nice new unbroken roof cheap...<P>I was gonna change the one on my forum but sold it and bought a t-top instead...<P>Good luck to all of you...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
